2026-09-07T22:35:00Z RESULT: Tested both improvement ideas from earlier discussion against the same 2024-09-08 to 2026-09-04 cached dataset (no new fetch needed) -- added a market-regime filter (SPY close > its own 50-day SMA, chosen over the more classic 200-day for warmup-cost reasons given the 2-year data window) to breakout/ema_cross, and added a third setup, mean_reversion (RSI(14) crossing up through 30, a confirmed oversold bounce not "still falling"). Results: regime-filtered breakout -0.22%/trade (14,137 trades, barely different from baseline -0.25%), regime-filtered ema_cross +0.05%/trade (10,335 trades, actually slightly WORSE than baseline +0.07%) -- the filter didn't help, largely because the market was bullish per this filter 338/451 days (~75%) in this window, so it wasn't very discriminating. mean_reversion (unfiltered): -0.17%/trade (8,294 trades) -- also negative, no better than the momentum setups. Verdict: none of the three approaches, with or without the regime filter, clear the "real edge" bar. ema_cross's baseline remains the least-bad result but this doesn't change that verdict. Code: scripts/massive_client.py gained get_ticker_range_aggs() (single-ticker historical range, one call vs grouped-daily's whole-market-per-day). scripts/backtest_ta.py gained _fetch_spy_regime(), _rsi_series(), a third "mean_reversion" signal in iter_signals(), and a new `compare` CLI command.
2026-09-07T22:50:00Z RESULT: Tested "combine TA signal with a catalyst" per user request. First confirmed live that FMP's free-tier earnings calendar has no historical lookback (402 Payment Required on any date more than ~a few weeks in the past) -- can't verify real news for 30,000+ historical signals at this tier. Used an overnight price gap (open vs prior close) as a data-derived PROXY for "a real catalyst happened" instead (genuine news usually gaps; routine drift usually doesn't) -- explicitly not the same as verified news, disclosed as such. Result: gap-confirmation made things WORSE, not better, and monotonically so as the threshold increased -- breakout -0.25% (baseline) -> -0.42% (>=2% gap) -> -0.57% (>=5% gap); ema_cross +0.07% (baseline) -> -0.12% (>=2%) -> -0.54% (>=5%). Coherent explanation: since entry is simulated at the NEXT day's open (never same-day), requiring a big gap on the signal day means buying AFTER the initial reaction, often near the top of the pop -- the same "sell the news"/overextension pattern already seen repeatedly in this session's discretionary research (DOCU, AEHR). This cross-validates that pattern quantitatively rather than contradicting it. Not promoting any gap-filtered variant. A more promising version of "combine with catalyst" would need to catch the catalyst BEFORE the reaction (forward earnings-date lookahead, matching screen.md's existing pre-catalyst design) rather than confirming it after -- not backtestable historically at FMP's free tier, would need forward paper-trading data instead. Code: added _gap_pct() and require_gap_pct param to backtest_ta.py's run_backtest(), extended `compare` command to include 2%/5% gap variants.
